  "date": "2026-10-29",
  "asof": "2026-10-30 11:10 UTC",
  "headline": "Alphabet fell 12% on its worst day in two decades \u2014 and GOOG gapped through your stop at the open",
  "standfirst": "Alphabet's Class C shares fell 12.29% to 282.32 after Wednesday's miss, taking the Nasdaq down 1.38% and the S&P 0.30%, while the Russell rose 1.01% as money rotated into health care, staples and smaller companies. September PCE matched forecasts at 3.6% headline and 3.1% core, Q3 GDP grew 3.4%, and markets kept a December hike above 80%. After the close Amazon narrowly missed, grew AWS 39%, showed trailing free cash flow of minus $42.4bn and fell about 7%. In the book GOOG was closed at the open, 283.68, below the 305.67 stop, for -42.18 and -2.09R. The day -38.21; Q4 -7.54, all realised, nothing open.",
